# Story page: frost
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = Frostbite Fjord
---
Down from the peaks, the world went white and quiet and terribly slippery.

On the fjord's ice {name} could not turn at all. It simply slid, with great dignity and no control, which is how I have conducted most of my life.

Frozen into a drift was an hourglass with its sand stopped mid-fall. When {name} touched it, everything else stopped too. Everything except {name}. I envied it enormously.
